[For "black"]
[Kind "main"]
[Start "caro-hillbilly 3...cxd5"]
[Name "Hillbilly Attack: 4.Bb5+"]

4. Bb5+ { The other way out for the bishop, with a check. }
4... Bd7 { Blocks with the bishop. It offers the swap and gives White nothing to attack. }
5. Bxd7+ { White's only active piece comes off. }
( 5. Bd3? { Keeps the bishops, but the bishop has now moved four times and blocks the d-pawn. }
  5... e5 { Black has the whole centre for nothing. White has given up a tempo and has no pawns in the middle. Nothing is won yet: the gain is the centre and the time. [%cal Gd5d4,Ge5e4] } )
5... Nxd7 { Takes back with a developing move. }
6. Nf3 Ngf6 { Develops; the knight guards d5 so that ...e6 is not forced. }
7. O-O e6 { Solid. The bishop on f8 can now come out. }
8. d4 Bd6 { The bishop's best diagonal. Black castles next, and is already a little better with the half-open c-file to use. } *
